   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 1. Load and Transform our Data\n",
    "\n",
    "We'll be using PyTorch's [ImageFolder](https://pytorch.org/vision/main/generated/torchvision.datasets.ImageFolder.html) class which makes is very easy to load data from a directory. For example, the training images are all stored in a directory path that looks like this:\n",
    "```\n",
    "root/class_1/xxx.png\n",
    "root/class_1/xxy.png\n",
    "root/class_1/xxz.png\n",
    "\n",
    "root/class_2/123.png\n",
    "root/class_2/nsdf3.png\n",
    "root/class_2/asd932_.png\n",
    "```\n",
    "\n",
    "Where, in this case, the root folder for training is `flowers/train/` and the classes are the names of flower types."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 4,
   "metadata": {
    "collapsed": true
   },
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# define training and test data directories\n",
    "train_dir = os.path.join(data_dir, 'train')\n",
    "test_dir = os.path.join(data_dir, 'test')\n",
    "\n",
    "# classes are folders in each directory with these names\n",
    "classes = ['daisy', 'dandelion', 'roses', 'sunflowers', 'tulips']"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Transforming the Data\n",
    "\n",
    "When we perform transfer learning, we have to shape our input data into the shape that the pre-trained model expects. VGG16 expects `224`-dim square images as input and so, we resize each flower image to fit this mold.\n",
    "\n",
    "Here we define the train and test data transformations. We will need at least resizing and converting to tensor, potentially also data augmentation. We load and transform the train and test data afterwards using `ImageFolder`. \n",
    "\n",
    "Note that we apply data augmentation only to the training images, not to the test data!"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 5,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "Num training images:  3130\n",
      "Num test images:  540\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "# VGG-16 takes 224x224 images as input, so we resize all of them\n",
    "train_transform = transforms.Compose([\n",
    "    transforms.RandomResizedCrop(224),\n",
    "    transforms.RandomHorizontalFlip(),\n",
    "    transforms.ToTensor(),\n",
    "])\n",
    "\n",
    "# make sure to use the same transformations for the test set, except data augmentation\n",
    "test_transform = transforms.Compose([\n",
    "    transforms.Resize(256),\n",
    "    transforms.CenterCrop(224),\n",
    "    transforms.ToTensor(),\n",
    "])\n",
    "\n",
    "# load and transform data using ImageFolder\n",
    "train_data = datasets.ImageFolder(train_dir, transform=train_transform)\n",
    "test_data = datasets.ImageFolder(test_dir, transform=test_transform)\n",
    "\n",
    "# print out some data stats\n",
    "print('Num training images: ', len(train_data))\n",
    "print('Num test images: ', len(test_data))"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### DataLoaders and Data Visualization"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 6,
   "metadata": {
    "collapsed": true
   },
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# define dataloader parameters\n",
    "batch_size = 20\n",
    "\n",
    "# prepare data loaders\n",
    "train_loader = torch.utils.data.DataLoader(train_data, batch_size=batch_size, shuffle=True)\n",
    "test_loader = torch.utils.data.DataLoader(test_data, batch_size=batch_size, shuffle=True)"
   ]
  },
