  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 10,
   "metadata": {
    "collapsed": true
   },
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Freeze training for all \"features\" layers\n",
    "for param in vgg16.features.parameters():\n",
    "    param.requires_grad = False\n",
    "    "
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "\n",
    "### Final Classifier Layer\n",
    "\n",
    "Once we have the pre-trained feature extractor, we just need to modify and/or add to the final, fully-connected classifier layers. In this case, we repace the last layer in the vgg classifier group of layers. \n",
    "\n",
    "This layer should see as input the number of features produced by the portion of the network that you are not changing, and produce an appropriate number of outputs for the flower classification task.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "Note that we can access any layer in a pretrained network by name and (sometimes) number, i.e. `vgg16.classifier[6]` is the sixth layer in a group of layers named \"classifier\"."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 11,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "5\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "# add a last linear layer  that maps n_inputs -> 5 flower classes\n",
    "# new layers automatically have requires_grad = True\n",
    "import torch.nn as nn\n",
    "n_inputs = vgg16.classifier[6].in_features\n",
    "\n",
    "last_layer = nn.Linear(n_inputs, len(classes))\n",
    "\n",
    "vgg16.classifier[6] = last_layer\n",
    "\n",
    "# after completing your model, if GPU is available, move the model to GPU\n",
    "if train_on_gpu:\n",
    "    vgg16.cuda()\n",
    "\n",
    "# check to see that your last layer produces the expected number of outputs\n",
    "print(vgg16.classifier[6].out_features)"
   ]
  },
