   "source": [
    "## 3. Training - [Loss Function](http://pytorch.org/docs/stable/nn.html#loss-functions) and [Optimizer](http://pytorch.org/docs/stable/optim.html)\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "Now we set up an advanced optimizer. See [here](http://pytorch.org/docs/stable/optim.html) for more details. We choose an SGD optimizer with momentum and name it `optimizer`. Also, we add a learning rate scheduler and name it `scheduler`.\n",
    "\n",
    "Note that the optimizer accepts as input _only_ the trainable parameters `vgg.classifier.parameters()`!"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 13,
   "metadata": {
    "collapsed": true
   },
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import torch.optim as optim\n",
    "\n",
    "# specify loss function (categorical cross-entropy)\n",
    "criterion = nn.CrossEntropyLoss()\n",
    "\n",
    "# specify optimizer (stochastic gradient descent) with learning rate = 0.001, momentum = 0.9\n",
    "# Note: The optimizer is only applied to the parameters of the last layer\n",
    "optimizer = optim.SGD(vgg16.classifier.parameters(), lr=0.001, momentum=0.9)\n",
    "\n",
    "# add an exponential learning rate scheduler with gamma = 0.9\n",
    "from torch.optim.lr_scheduler import ExponentialLR\n",
    "scheduler = ExponentialLR(optimizer, gamma=0.9) # learning rate decay: reduce LR by 10% every epoch"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
